+---
+"@elata-biosciences/rppg-web": minor
+---
+
+New `rgbPulse` option on `RppgProcessor`, passed on by `createRppgSession`.
+With `rgbPulse: "pos"` the processor builds the pulse its own estimators read
+from colour samples (`pushSampleRgb`, `pushSampleRgbMeta`) with POS and the
+0.7 to 4 Hz band-pass, designed for the rate the samples arrive at. The
+default, `"chrom"`, is the previous behaviour, unchanged: channel gain, then
+`ChromPulseModel`, with the raw green value kept for the first nine samples
+and whenever CHROM gives about 0. Those raw values are about a hundred grey
+levels beside a pulse of about 0.01 and stay in the 45 s window, and CHROM's
+axes keep a constant part that puts the frame-to-frame change of its weight in
+the heart-rate band, so on a clean synthetic pulse the processor's spectral
+estimate reads the same rate whatever the true rate and `bpm` is withheld or
+wrong. With `"pos"` both read the true rate. `"chrom"` stays the default because with no
+pulse at all `"pos"` reports `bpm` in more seconds at 30 frames a second. A
+session feeds colour samples for every frame it does not fuse (no face mesh,
+`multiRoiFusion` or `useSkinMask` off, or no face region with skin); fused
+samples never take this path.
diff --git a/packages/rppg-web/README.md b/packages/rppg-web/README.md
index 9a34403..8ebde48 100644
--- a/packages/rppg-web/README.md
+++ b/packages/rppg-web/README.md
@@ -600,6 +600,16 @@ available:
 - `RppgProcessor` for direct sample ingestion
 - `DemoRunner`, `MediaPipeFrameSource`, and `MediaPipeFaceFrameSource` for advanced browser control
 
+`RppgProcessor` passes colour samples (`pushSampleRgb`, `pushSampleRgbMeta`) to
+the WASM core and also reads them with its own estimators. Pass
+`{ rgbPulse: "pos" }` as its fourth argument, or to `createRppgSession`, to
+build the pulse those estimators read with POS and a 0.7 to 4 Hz band-pass at
+the rate the samples arrive at. The default, `"chrom"`, keeps the previous
+signal, which reads a clean synthetic pulse at the wrong rate; it stays the
+default because with no pulse at all `"pos"` reports a rate in more seconds. A
+session feeds colour samples for every frame it does not fuse (no face mesh,
+`multiRoiFusion` or `useSkinMask` off, or no face region with skin).
+
 For most browser apps, prefer `createRppgSession()` and only drop lower if you
 need custom lifecycle or rendering behavior.
 
